1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,119
Before sunrise, a shipment is ready to leave.

2
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:10,178
For the team behind it, the job is bigger than moving freight.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,866
It's keeping a promise across a continent.

4
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:20,573
Then the conditions change.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,555
A weather warning.

6
00:00:22,555 --> 00:00:24,319
Rising rainfall.

7
00:00:24,319 --> 00:00:25,902
A rail update.

8
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,831
Separate signals.

9
00:00:27,831 --> 00:00:29,775
One decision to make.

10
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:34,973
Atlas IQ's Corridor Lifeline concept brings those signals
together.

11
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:42,211
So the team can review the risk, rethink the shipment plan, and
prepare the paperwork.

12
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,664
An emergency permit draft.

13
00:00:44,664 --> 00:00:46,511
A clear risk summary.

14
00:00:46,511 --> 00:00:48,928
Ready for a person to review.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,541
The weather is beyond our control.

16
00:00:51,541 --> 00:00:53,972
Preparation doesn't have to be.

17
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:55,775
Atlas IQ.

18
00:00:55,775 --> 00:00:57,816
Anticipate disruption.

19
00:00:57,816 --> 00:00:59,650
Prepare your response.
